   "problem": "A sample of $n = 25$ has $\\bar{x} = 50$; the population has $\\sigma = 10$. Using $z^* = 2$, give the 95% confidence interval for $\\mu$.",
   "answer": "$(46, 54)$",
   "solution_sketch": "$\\operatorname{SE} = 10/5 = 2$; margin $= 2 \\cdot 2 = 4$; interval $50 \\pm 4$."
